    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0286" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/993: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bailly-Blanchard</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-27T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                                1921—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Department’s No. 82, September 27, 6 p.m., No. 89, October 11, 6 p.m., No. 94,
                    October 18, 6 p.m., and No. 1, January 5, 1 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d184-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>The Department is unable to understand why no reply has been received from you to
                    above cable instructions to report to Department the modifications recommended
                    by you and the Treaty officials interested in the laws or projects mentioned in
                    your August 20, 11 a.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d184-f2"/></p>
                <p>It is necessary for the Department to have this report prior to arriving at a
                    decision upon this subject, and unless you have already forwarded such report
                    you will do so immediately by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
